==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}}, late 14th century, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|indigence|lang=fro}} (13th century), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|indigentia|lang=la}}, from {{term|indigentem|lang=la}}, form of {{term|indigere||to need|lang=la}}, from {{term|indu||in, within|lang=la}} + {{term|egere||be in need, want|lang=la}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Only relation to antonym {{term|affluence|lang=en}} is common Latinate suffix {{suffix||ence}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[extreme]] [[poverty]] or [[destitution]]

